/* progress.vh -- THE PER-LANE LIVENESS WATCHDOG, included by every bench.
 *
 * ⛔⛔⛔ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND IT IS THE SHARPEST LESSON OF THE ARC. The
 * first self-clocked SHIFT build retired a clocked SHIFT after ONE dispatch
 * instead of sixteen, and ALL 75 SWEEP ARMS PASSED ON IT. Every bench's
 * success criterion was that pins MOVE -- `uio_oe` toggles, a trace is
 * non-empty -- and an action that retires early moves pins beautifully. The
 * defect was found by COVERAGE (the COLLECT phase's branch count was 0 in all
 * twelve benches), not by any bench.
 * ⇒ "The pins moved" is a VACUOUS success criterion. Progress is the real one,
 *   and nothing was asserting it.
 *
 * ⛔⛔ TWO LAYERS, AND THE SPLIT IS A RULING, NOT A STYLE CHOICE.
 *
 *   LAYER A -- universal liveness, COARSE, and deliberately independent of the
 *   golden model. Every lane's PC keeps advancing; no lane sits on one action
 *   past a generous bound; the writeback and retire counters are non-zero. It
 *   is crude on purpose, so it CANNOT be wrong in the same way the model could
 *   be: the model must not be its own only witness.
 *
 *   LAYER B -- exact per-action conformance. IT LIVES IN
 *   `test/clocked_conform.vh` AND SHIPS WITH THE CLOCKED RTL, not here,
 *   because its "is this a clocked action" predicate is `clk_real & level`
 *   -- which only MEANS self-clocked in the new engine. Landed earlier it
 *   would mis-fire on the pre-clocked corpus, and an `ifdef` nobody defines
 *   is a check that never runs, which is the very thing this file is about.
 *   It checks against `clocked_bounds.vh`,
 *   which is GENERATED by `model/clocked_phase.py` from measured runs. The
 *   model is the single authority for exact counts and NO BOUND IS RECOMPUTED
 *   HERE -- not even the SHIFT/SHIFTIN off-by-one (`OP_SHIFT` counts
 *   `a_cnt + 1` bits, `OP_SHIFTIN` counts `a_cnt`), because a constant written
 *   twice is this project's most expensive recurring defect.
 *
 * ⛔ WHAT IS DELIBERATELY EXEMPT, and why it is not a hole: a CHAINING
 * `OP_REARM` (op = REARM, level = 0) re-dispatches for ever BY DESIGN -- it is
 * ruling 2's mechanism for delays longer than the delay field, and it is how
 * every parked lane waits. A watchdog that failed on it would fire on every
 * bench in the suite, and the "fix" would be to delete the watchdog. So this
 * does NOT assert "every lane's PC always advances" unconditionally; it
 * asserts the thing that is actually always true.
 *
 * ⛔⛔ A TRAP THIS FILE FELL INTO AND MUST NOT AGAIN: the hook first read
 * `dut.u_eng.st === dut.u_eng.ST_WB`. A HIERARCHICAL REFERENCE TO A LOCALPARAM
 * compiled without complaint and the comparison was NEVER TRUE -- so the
 * watchdog ran on all twelve benches and checked nothing. A check that cannot
 * fire reads exactly like a check that passed. It is written as the literal
 * `2'd2`, with the encoding cited: `src/pe_engine.v` has
 * `localparam [1:0] ST_IDLE = 2'd0, ST_DRIVE = 2'd1, ST_WB = 2'd2`.
 * ⭐ The writeback counter in `pg_report` is what made that vacuity VISIBLE,
 * and it stays: "0 writebacks seen" must look different from "passed".
 *
 * ⛔⛔ AND A SECOND VACUITY TRAP IN THIS SAME FILE: every `$display` whose
 * format string was built by BRACE CONCATENATION -- `$display({"a %0d ",
 * "b %0d"}, x, y)` -- printed NOTHING AT ALL, while the counter beside it
 * incremented 144 times. A failure that counts itself and says nothing is
 * indistinguishable from a pass to anyone reading the log. ⇒ EVERY FORMAT
 * STRING HERE IS A SINGLE PLAIN LITERAL, however long the line.
 * ⭐ Both traps in this file had the same shape -- a check that cannot speak --
 * and both were caught only by comparing a COUNTER against the messages.
 *
 * ⭐ IT REPORTS BY PRINTING `FAIL`, which wires it into the existing machinery
 * for free: `test/coverage_sweep.sh` greps each arm's log for a case-sensitive
 * `FAIL`. And it self-reports in a `final` block, so no bench has to remember
 * to call anything -- a watchdog that only speaks when invited is silent in
 * exactly the bench nobody updated.
 *
 * USAGE:   `include "test/progress.vh"      // after the `dut` instance
 */

// ⛔ A DECLARED UPPER BOUND, not a second copy of N_LANES. The watchdog never
// iterates lanes -- it only touches the lane in `cur` -- so this sizes storage
// and nothing else. A lane index beyond it is REPORTED, not silently dropped.
localparam integer PG_MAXL  = 8;
// LAYER A's generous bound: far above any legitimate clocked action (the
// longest is a 17-dispatch 8-bit clocked receive), so layer A fires only on a
// genuine hang and never merely because layer B's table changed.
localparam integer PG_COARSE = 64;

integer pg_n     [0:PG_MAXL-1];      // writebacks on the current action
integer pg_pc    [0:PG_MAXL-1];      // the PC they were at
integer pg_fa;
integer pg_wbs, pg_acts;
integer pg_k;
reg     pg_oor;

initial begin
  for (pg_k = 0; pg_k < PG_MAXL; pg_k = pg_k + 1) begin
    pg_n[pg_k] = 0;  pg_pc[pg_k] = -1;
  end
  pg_fa = 0;
  pg_wbs = 0;  pg_acts = 0;
  pg_oor = 1'b0;
end

always @(posedge dut.clk) begin
  if (dut.rst_n !== 1'b1) begin
    for (pg_k = 0; pg_k < PG_MAXL; pg_k = pg_k + 1) begin
      pg_n[pg_k] = 0;  pg_pc[pg_k] = -1;
    end
  end else if (dut.u_eng.st === 2'd2) begin        // ST_WB -- literal, see above
    pg_wbs = pg_wbs + 1;
    if (dut.u_eng.cur >= PG_MAXL) begin
      if (!pg_oor) begin
        pg_oor = 1'b1;
        $display("FAIL progress.vh: lane index %0d exceeds PG_MAXL=%0d -- the watchdog cannot see every lane; raise PG_MAXL rather than trust a partial check", dut.u_eng.cur, PG_MAXL);
        pg_fa = pg_fa + 1;
      end
    end else if (dut.u_eng.a_op === 3'd7 && dut.u_eng.a_lvl === 1'b0) begin
      pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur]  = 0;                   // the chaining re-arm
      pg_pc[dut.u_eng.cur] = dut.u_eng.l_pc[dut.u_eng.cur];
    end else begin
      if (pg_pc[dut.u_eng.cur] !== dut.u_eng.l_pc[dut.u_eng.cur]) begin
        // the PC moved: the previous action at this lane has RETIRED
        if (pg_pc[dut.u_eng.cur] !== -1) pg_acts = pg_acts + 1;
        pg_pc[dut.u_eng.cur]  = dut.u_eng.l_pc[dut.u_eng.cur];
        pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur]   = 1;
      end else begin
        pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur] = pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur] + 1;
      end
      // ---- LAYER A: coarse liveness, model-independent -------------------
      if (pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur] == PG_COARSE + 1) begin
        $display("FAIL progress.vh[A]: lane %0d has sat on the action at pc=%0d for %0d dispatches (coarse bound %0d) -- it is NOT RETIRING", dut.u_eng.cur, pg_pc[dut.u_eng.cur], pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur], PG_COARSE);
        pg_fa = pg_fa + 1;
      end
    end
  end
end

task pg_report;
  begin
    // ⛔ DID-NOT-RUN MUST NOT LOOK LIKE PASSED. These two counters exist
    // because this file was once vacuous on every bench and said nothing.
    $display("  progress.vh[A]: %0d writeback(s), %0d action(s) retired",
             pg_wbs, pg_acts);
    if (pg_wbs == 0)
      $display("FAIL progress.vh: no writeback was ever observed, so the liveness check had nothing to check");
    else if (pg_acts == 0)
      $display("FAIL progress.vh: no action was observed to retire, so the liveness check had nothing to check");
    else if (pg_fa == 0)
      $display("  progress.vh[A]: ok -- coarse liveness clean");
    else
      $display("FAIL progress.vh[A]: %0d liveness failure(s)", pg_fa);
  end
endtask

final begin
  pg_report;
end
